<tr><td><h1>The Quiet Letter</h1><h2>Issue 12: Libraries</h2>
<p>Public libraries are one of the few places where you can stay as long as=
 you like without buying anything. This issue is about what that does for r=
eading.</p>
<p>We visited three small branch libraries and asked the staff what people =
read when nobody is watching. The answers were surprising: poetry, repair m=
anuals, and long novels.</p>
<blockquote>A library is a quiet argument that time spent reading is time w=
ell spent.</blockquote>
<p>Next week: walking and thinking.</p></td></tr>
